-- title:
--   Rank-one generator for n-torsion of a fake elliptic curve
-- statement:
--   Fix $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and primes $q,q'$, and assume `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'`: the quaternion algebra $B=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ satisfies $a>0$ or $b>0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of the integers of $\mathbb{Q}$ the completion $B\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra (every nonzero element is a unit) exactly when $v$ contains $q$ or $q'$. Let $\Lambda\subseteq B$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is a maximal order, i.e. it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, is finitely generated, spans $B$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and is maximal for inclusion among such submodules. Let $N\in\mathbb{N}$, let $K$ be an algebraically closed field, and let $E$ be a fake elliptic curve over $K$ with $\Lambda$-action and level $N$: a scheme $A$ with structure morphism $f$ to $\operatorname{Spec}K$, a commutative relative group law $L$, the abelian-scheme property bundle (smooth, proper, connected fibres, a group law exists), fibres of topological Krull dimension $2$, a map $m\mapsto E.\mathrm{act}\,m$ from $\Lambda$ to endomorphisms over the base which is unital, multiplicative, additive on points and satisfies the trace normalisation, together with the auxiliary curve and level data. Let $n$ be prime with $n\neq 0$ in $K$. Then there is a point $P_0$ of $A$ over $\operatorname{Spec}K$ (a section of $f$, in the Lean formulation a morphism $\operatorname{Spec}K\to A$ composing with $f$ to the identity) such that: the $n$-fold iterated group-law sum $nP_0$ is the identity section; every $K$-point $P$ with $nP$ the identity equals $P_0$ followed by $E.\mathrm{act}\,m$ for some $m\in\Lambda$; and for $m\in\Lambda$, $P_0$ followed by $E.\mathrm{act}\,m$ is the identity section if and only if $m=n\,m'$ in $B$ for some $m'\in\Lambda$.
--
--   This is the statement that the $n$-torsion $A[n](K)$ of a fake elliptic curve is a free module of rank one over $\Lambda/n\Lambda$, generated by $P_0$; in particular $\#A[n](K)=n^4$. It is the input for the classification of $\Lambda$-stable subgroups of $A[n](K)$ and hence for the construction and enumeration of extra level structures at primes in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting, and it is cited in the rigidity statement that an automorphism acting as multiplication by an integer on points is trivial.
